course: dictionary
lesson: 10813
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and vault is one of them. The words around it show you which meaning the writer means. «The robbers tried to break into the bank vault full of gold.» Here a vault is a strong, locked room for keeping money and treasure safe.
explain: «In PE, Mia had to vault over the box.» Here vault is a verb. It means to jump over something, pushing off with your hands. Check by swapping in jump over: «Mia had to jump over the box» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Vault can also mean an arched roof or ceiling, as in an old church, or a room under a building that was sometimes used for burying people. When you meet a word you already know, stop and ask: does my meaning fit this sentence? If it does not, try another meaning from the list.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is needed.
fact: «Vault» can mean a strong, locked room for keeping money and treasure safe, as in a bank.
fact: «Vault» can also mean to jump over something, pushing off with your hands or with a pole.
fact: The Svalbard Global Seed Vault in Norway keeps over a million seed samples inside a frozen mountain, because cold and dryness keep seeds alive for a very long time.
fact: In gymnastics you may vault over a vaulting box, and in athletics there is the pole vault.
exercise: «The robbers tried to break into the bank vault full of gold.» What is a vault here? | A kind of jump in PE | *A strong, locked room for keeping money and treasure safe | A tall, thin tree | A loud noise in the night
exercise: «In PE, Mia had to vault over the box.» What does vault mean here? | To sit down quietly | *To jump over something, pushing off with her hands | To climb down a rope | To sleep under a roof
exercise: «The old church had a high vaulted ceiling.» What does vaulted describe? | A wooden floor | *A ceiling shaped like an arch | A window made of glass | A church bell
test: «Quetzalcoatlus probably vaulted into the air with its strong arms.» What does vaulted mean here? | Buried under the ground | *Jumped up, pushing off | Locked away safely | Sang loudly
test: «The Svalbard Global Seed Vault in Norway stores over a million seed samples.» What is the vault here? | To jump over a fence | A ceiling shaped like an arch | A room for a school play | *A strong, locked store for keeping things safe
exam: Which sentence uses vault to mean jump? | *«Tom will vault the fence on his bike.» | «The bank vault was locked at night.» | «The seed vault is deep in a frozen mountain.» | «The old church had a vaulted roof.»
